@*
    Aim at a job.

    A COPY OF JobSpecActivity: the lead paragraph, a six-line box to paste the
    advert into, one primary button, and the result underneath.

    THE MODEL CHOOSES IDS, NOT WORDS. It is asked which of the facts already in the
    profile to lead with, so the output can only ever be a reordering of what
    somebody actually said about themselves. A CV that improves itself is a CV that
    lies in an interview.
*@
@page "/job-spec"
@inject IJobSpecTailor Tailor
@inject IShareTarget Share
@inject IFormFactor Host

@*
    THE WHATSAPP SENTENCE ONLY WHERE IT IS TRUE. This screen promised "share it
    here from WhatsApp" on both hosts, and the hybrid had no intent filter at all
    - Circle AI never appeared in the share sheet, so only the pasting half was
    ever true. The filter exists now; a browser tab still has no share sheet, and
    says the half it can keep.
*@
<p class="lead">
    @(Host.IsOnDevice
        ? "Paste the advert, or share it here from WhatsApp."
        : "Paste the advert here.")
    Your CV will be rearranged to put the parts that match it first — using only
    what you already told me.
</p>

@* Same as the CV answer box: a controlled value re-applied per keystroke
   drops characters out of what somebody typed. *@
<textarea class="spec" rows="6" placeholder="Paste the job advert here"
          aria-label="The job advert"
          @bind="_advert" @bind:event="oninput"></textarea>

@*
    DISABLED UNTIL THERE IS AN ADVERT. It ran on an empty box - pressing it with
    nothing pasted spent the model on nothing and came back with nothing, which
    reads as the feature being broken rather than as the box being empty.
*@
<button class="go" @onclick="Run" disabled="@(_busy || _advert.Trim().Length == 0)">@_action</button>

@if (_out.Length > 0)
{
    @* pre-line, because the result carries its own paragraph breaks. *@
    <div class="out">@_out</div>
}

@code {
    string _advert = "";
    string _out = "";
    string _action = "Aim my CV at this job";
    bool _busy;

    /// <summary>Take an advert somebody shared in from another app.</summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// The whole point of the share target: arriving this way must require no
    /// typing at all, so the advert is already in the box and the only thing
    /// left to do is press the button.
    /// </remarks>
    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        if (Share.Take() is { Length: > 0 } shared)
        {
            _advert = shared;
            _out = "Advert received. Tap to aim your CV at it.";
        }
    }

    async Task Run()
    {
        if (_busy) return;
        _busy = true;
        _action = "Reading the advert…";

        var progress = new Progress<string>(line =>
        {
            _action = line;
            StateHasChanged();
        });

        try
        {
            var result = await Tailor.TailorAsync(_advert, progress);
            _out = result.Text;
            _action = result.Ok ? "Aim at another job" : "Try again";
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            _out = $"Could not read that advert. ({ex.GetType().Name})";
            _action = "Try again";
        }
        finally
        {
            _busy = false;
        }
    }
}
